{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals","id":584885,"title":"Were-Elementals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T11:02:38-07:00","id":584885,"title":"Were-Elementals?","content":"I was browsing through another topic in this forum that mentioned how Pangaea's spirit-gods didn't just include an animal menagerie, but various gods of natural features and elemental forces. It got me thinking: what if, out there, there was something similar to the children of Mother Moon, but their spirit-halves came from an elemental coupling rather than one of beast and moon? I can see something like a group of Helios-sired &quot;fire-shifters&quot; that have a human, a flame-person, and living flame forms, ploughing over forests and tearing into buildings in whatever may count as their form of death rage. Or maybe something water-based, also children of Luna when she consorted with an ancient god of the sea.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T11:31:56-07:00","id":584928,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I like the idea. I was thinking about storm children and dream kin. They wouldn't necessarily have to be based around Luna, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:27:57-07:00","id":585919,"title":"","content":"Could probably use the Claimed rules, unless you wanted to come up with a ton of Gifts (or co-opt werewolf ones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:58:19-07:00","id":586173,"title":"","content":"It would be nice to build some micro templates for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:16:27-07:00","id":586203,"title":"","content":"<i>World of Darkness: Genasi</i>? I'd play that. I think I'll start putting together a pitch/first draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:54:54-07:00","id":586223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586203#post586203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>World of Darkness: Genasi</i>? I'd play that. I think I'll start putting together a pitch/first draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh frig yes I'd play that too. Elemental hybrids in WoD fit as much as glue does to paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:09:36-07:00","id":586229,"title":"","content":"oWoD had something like this in their Possessed sourcebook. Between the Kami and the Gorgons, you could make some elemental-types pretty well. Obviously not the same as this. I would be interested in collaborating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:13:40-07:00","id":586232,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Okay, I've got a &quot;pitch&quot; as it were. It's unpolished as hell, but I hope y'all can see what I'm going for.<br /> <br /> Despite using some Freudian terminology, since this is a werewolf-related game, remember that I'm aiming for a sister game to our beloved Forsaken:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Elemental: The Prime</span></u></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">A Storytelling Game of the </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N3472Q6kvg0\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><u>Laws of Nature</u></span></a></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The World of Darkness is already full of creatures who are beholden to primal instinct: the Kindred and their Beasts, the Uratha and their Spirit halves, the Begotten and their Horrors, to name but a few. These instincts and drives are based on living impulses, however. They represent life. The Prime represent nature itself. Their drives are not born of the puerile meanderings of sentience, but of the fundamental aspects of the universe.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Theme:</b> The Id Ascendant. Characters are the expressions of nature given human form. Their true selves do not have desires or needs -- they </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>were</i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, they </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>are</i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, and they </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>will be</i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Mood:</b> Natural disaster. Earthquakes. Wildfires. Tsunamis. Hurricanes. When a Prime allows themselves to be unleashed, they leave destruction in their wake. This applies as much to friendships and families as it does to the shattered streets.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:18:43-07:00","id":586241,"title":"","content":"I would use Prim<i>al</i>, not Prime. Prime means &quot;first&quot;, primal has the connotation you seem to be looking for. Primeval is also good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:22:41-07:00","id":586244,"title":"","content":"I was trying to go for something meaning &quot;base&quot; or &quot;fundamental&quot;. First isn't quite it, but Primal and Primeval sound too....well, I get put in the mind of dinosaurs and Conan: The Barbarian. Plus Beast has The Primordial, so I didn't want it to sound too similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:23:33-07:00","id":586245,"title":"","content":"Dreaded double post.<br /> <br /> I think one thing that needs to be absolutely clear here is <i>what is and what isn't an element</i> within the context of the game. And it needs to be very clear. Are we limiting them? Are we providing a guideline? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:25:10-07:00","id":586246,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest picking a different title and using The Elemental as a sub-title, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:26:04-07:00","id":586247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586245#post586245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreaded double post.<br /> <br /> I think one thing that needs to be absolutely clear here is <i>what is and what isn't an element</i> within the context of the game. And it needs to be very clear. Are we limiting them? Are we providing a guideline? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good question. I had assumed the four elementals that you can obtain through Gift of the Elements as a starting point: Fire, Air, Water, Earth. Classic Roman four. I'm all for altering them.<br /> <br /> Oooh, better idea for a subtitle:<br /> <br /> Elemental: The Cataclysm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:38:10-07:00","id":586253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586247#post586247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a good question. I had assumed the four elementals that you can obtain through Gift of the Elements as a starting point: Fire, Air, Water, Earth. Classic Roman four. I'm all for altering them.<br /> <br /> Oooh, better idea for a subtitle:<br /> <br /> Elemental: The Cataclysm</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the four &quot;sub-elements&quot; based on that system, IIRC: hot, cold, wet and dry. That could be used to determine the secondary splat: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classical_element#/media/File:Four_elements_representation.svg\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classi...esentation.svg</a><br /> <br /> I also recommend this for ideas with the &quot;id ascendant&quot;: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TyyE8c27-9Y\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TyyE8c27-9Y</a><br /> <br /> And I like that title, and the pitch you have so far! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:41:56-07:00","id":586256,"title":"","content":"Elemental: The Catalysts. Because they catalyze things! Nature's wrath! Maybe their aim is to start shit.<br /> <br /> And that's a pretty narrow scope. I mean we're obviously going with classical elements, not periodic elements. But &quot;wood&quot; should probably not be lumped in with &quot;earth&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would be okay with with Earth, Air, Fire, Water, and Wood (a la Exalted). My concern is that this will make their powers very particular of their element. No one is likely to have the fire-themed powers <i>except for Fire Elementals</i>. But that may be a feature, not a bug, and <i>largely</i> depends on how the powers are designed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:55:56-07:00","id":586266,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of using &quot;sub-elements&quot;, especially in lieu of the &quot;base&quot; elements.<br /> <br /> Wood...I dunno, I'm not married to using 5 splats, and I can't think of any good disasters related to wood.<br /> <br /> Power-wise, I think something like the Geist Keys/Manifestations is a good starting point. You want to allow all of the characters a thematic reason to pick a splat, but you want them to be able to apply the powers in a variety of ways irrespective of their splat choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:58:36-07:00","id":586268,"title":"","content":"Make an X splat and a Y splat. The X splat is fire, air, earth, water and wood. The Y splat is <i>also</i> fire, air earth water and wood. <br /> <br /> So you'd have mud elementals and steam elementals and burning tree elementals and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:03:00-07:00","id":586272,"title":"","content":"I think Elfive's idea is actually pretty neat. Air + Fire can be Lightning, Earth + Water is Mud.<br /> <br /> I can understand how Wood doesn't really bring up thoughts of cataclysm. I could see just the four classical elements juxtaposed against each other. Earth + Fire = Metal.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Tolerance Trait: <b>Vim.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 07-10-2015, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:09:27-07:00","id":586278,"title":"","content":"Please, everyone:<br /> <br /> X Splats are Air, Earth, Fire, and Water<br /> Y Splats are Air, Earth, Fire, and Water<br /> Z Splats are Positive and Negative.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mimir.net/essays/planarphysics.html\" target=\"_blank\">I should go sit in my corner, shouldn't I?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:11:48-07:00","id":586281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586268#post586268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make an X splat and a Y splat. The X splat is fire, air, earth, water and wood. The Y splat is <i>also</i> fire, air earth water and wood.<br /> <br /> So you'd have mud elementals and steam elementals and burning tree elementals and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586272#post586272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Elfive's idea is actually pretty neat. Air + Fire can be Lightning, Earth + Water is Mud.<br /> <br /> I can understand how Wood doesn't really bring up thoughts of cataclysm. I could see just the four classical elements juxtaposed against each other. Earth + Fire = Metal.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Tolerance Trait: <b>Vim.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also like Elfive's idea. Should there be an option for picking the same X- and Y-splat? Inferno Elementals, Mountain Elementals, Ocean Elementals, Hurricane Elementals? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also like your name for the Supernatural Tolerance Trait, gebbethine: it's my favorite text editor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 07-10-2015, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:13:23-07:00","id":586282,"title":"","content":"Oh, of course. Can't have the system exclude the classics. That would just be wrong.<br /> <br /> Probably should have some sort of bonus to offset the lack of flexibility. Fire + Fire = EVEN MORE FIRE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 07-10-2015, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:14:31-07:00","id":586283,"title":"","content":"I think they should be able to double up, absolutely. Air + Air can be a twister, Fire + Fire is pure, unsatisfied flame. Earth + Earth can give you rare minerals, too, not just mountains. There should be several possibilities for any combination.<br /> <br /> I think rather than making their powers like Keys/Manifestations, it would be better to make them in the style of 2e Changeling.<br /> <br /> A power does X. HOW it does it depends on what you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:21:13-07:00","id":586287,"title":"","content":"Maybe make it so that the X-Splat represents the Elements as physical, world-shattering <i>things</i>, while the Y-splat represents that Element as a spiritual symbol, a higher calling that urges them to be something more than a humaniform disaster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:22:33-07:00","id":586288,"title":"","content":"You know...<br /> <br /> Water + Earth = Mud + Fire = Clay.<br /> <br /> *brainbreak*<br /> <br /> Special Merit option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:26:03-07:00","id":586291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586287#post586287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make it so that the X-Splat represents the Elements as physical, world-shattering <i>things</i>, while the Y-splat represents that Element as a spiritual symbol, a higher calling that urges them to be something more than a humaniform disaster?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think that would fall under the purview of the Virtue/Vice equivalent. I like the idea of retaining the dualistic, animistic qualities from Werewolf though. Makes it more interesting than just &quot;pick two X-splats&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:38:27-07:00","id":586296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals#post584885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was browsing through another topic in this forum that mentioned how Pangaea's spirit-gods didn't just include an animal menagerie, but various gods of natural features and elemental forces. It got me thinking: what if, out there, there was something similar to the children of Mother Moon, but their spirit-halves came from an elemental coupling rather than one of beast and moon? I can see something like a group of Helios-sired &quot;fire-shifters&quot; that have a human, a flame-person, and living flame forms, ploughing over forests and tearing into buildings in whatever may count as their form of death rage. Or maybe something water-based, also children of Luna when she consorted with an ancient god of the sea.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Pangaeans aren't just animals, they're symbols of natural cycles and forces - animals, weather, concepts, seasons and the like. Where spirits are a reflection of the world, Pangaeans were <i>pillars</i> of it.<br /> <br /> As for the exact nature of the relationship between Uratha and the Great Predator, and the other Pangaeans and any putative offspring they may have had, you'll have to wait for Dark Eras to be released <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:45:41-07:00","id":586361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586296#post586296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the Pangaeans aren't just animals, they're symbols of natural cycles and forces - animals, weather, concepts, seasons and the like. Where spirits are a reflection of the world, Pangaeans were <i>pillars</i> of it.<br /> <br /> As for the exact nature of the relationship between Uratha and the Great Predator, and the other Pangaeans and any putative offspring they may have had, you'll have to wait for Dark Eras to be released <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>*deep, heavy breathing*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:06:21-07:00","id":586835,"title":"","content":"Hmm, at tvtropes, it lists the common elements in fiction as-<br /> <br /> 1) Earth<br /> <br /> 2) Fire<br /> <br /> 3) Air<br /> <br /> 4) Water<br /> <br /> 5) Electricity<br /> <br /> 6) Ice<br /> <br /> 7) Light<br /> <br /> 8) Darkness<br /> <br /> 9) Wood, nature, life<br /> <br /> 10) Animals<br /> <br /> 11) Machines<br /> <br /> 12) Crystal<br /> <br /> 13) Death<br /> <br /> 14) Emotions<br /> <br /> 15) metal<br /> <br /> 16) spirits or souls<br /> <br /> 17) energy or magic<br /> <br /> 18) poison<br /> <br /> 19) lava<br /> <br /> 20) the sun<br /> <br /> 21) moon<br /> <br /> 22) star<br /> <br /> 23) sound<br /> <br /> 24) radiation<br /> <br /> 25) time<br /> <br /> 26) space or gravity<br /> <br /> 27) Void<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating using all of them, but which ones seem interesting and viable as options?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:27:15-07:00","id":586847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586835#post586835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not advocating using all of them, but which ones seem interesting and viable as options?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have to first define, due to the fact that we've had both Eastern and Greek elemental groupings presented as options: <b>what, in more universal terms, is an elemental</b>?<br /> <br /> According to Google's built-in dictionary:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> el\u00b7e\u00b7men\u00b7tal<br /> \u02ccel\u0259\u02c8men(t)l/<br /> adjective<br /> adjective: elemental<br /> 1.<br /> primary or basic.<br /> &quot;elemental features from which all other structures are compounded&quot;<br /> synonyms: basic, primary, fundamental, essential, root, underlying; rudimentary<br /> &quot;the elemental principles of accounting&quot;<br /> concerned with chemical elements or other basic components.<br /> &quot;elemental analysis&quot;<br /> consisting of a single chemical element.<br /> 2.<br /> related to or embodying the powers of nature.<br /> &quot;a thunderstorm is the inevitable outcome of battling elemental forces&quot;<br /> synonyms: natural, atmospheric, meteorological, environmental, climatic<br /> &quot;elemental forces&quot;<br /> (of an emotion) having the primitive and inescapable character of a force of nature.<br /> &quot;the urge for revenge was too elemental to be ignored&quot;<br /> synonyms: basic, primary, fundamental, essential, root, underlying; rudimentary<br /> &quot;the elemental principles of accounting&quot;<br /> noun<br /> noun: elemental; plural noun: elementals<br /> 1.<br /> a supernatural entity or force thought to be physically manifested by occult means. </div> </div> </div>So in this case, a were-elemental is something that takes the form of man <i>and</i> a primeval force of nature. Any powers involving plants, animals or living beings of any kind is out the window, as we are talking the most fundamental, more environmentally-oriented beings than a werewolf or werecreature might be. Were-elementals are natural phenomena like thunderstorms, landslides and magma flows that happen to walk, talk and grab a burger at Wendy's like everyone else does.<br /> <br /> So basically, any sort of natural weather and/or geological phenomena can be the form an elemental takes, IF we run with this definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T16:43:03-07:00","id":587497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=586847#post586847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we have to first define, due to the fact that we've had both Eastern and Greek elemental groupings presented as options: <b>what, in more universal terms, is an elemental</b>?<br /> <br /> According to Google's built-in dictionary:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So in this case, a were-elemental is something that takes the form of man <i>and</i> a primeval force of nature. Any powers involving plants, animals or living beings of any kind is out the window, as we are talking the most fundamental, more environmentally-oriented beings than a werewolf or werecreature might be. Were-elementals are natural phenomena like thunderstorms, landslides and magma flows that happen to walk, talk and grab a burger at Wendy's like everyone else does.<br /> <br /> So basically, any sort of natural weather and/or geological phenomena can be the form an elemental takes, IF we run with this definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am 100% behind this definition. It's basically where I was headed with the pitch, but if we drop the Four Elements design we can run with storm elementals, magma elementals, etc...<br /> <br /> Something gebbethine and I were pondering: playing around with Aspirations and Touchstones. The big defining feature would be &quot;indiscriminate&quot;. The werelementals develop very strong impulses to go after the things and people that they want or need. Kind of like being a werewolf on the Sacred Hunt <i>all the time</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T16:45:30-07:00","id":587499,"title":"","content":"My fiancee also likes the idea of were-tsunamis and were-earthquakes. Her response:<br /> <br /> &quot;A Makara Beast and a were-tsunami would make the perfect couple.&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;So in other words: were-Sharknado?&quot;<br /> &quot;That's their baby.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T17:41:26-07:00","id":587568,"title":"","content":"I'd ship it. *proceeds to be thrown out a window, climbs back in*<br /> <br /> So, if we drop the four elements splat idea, we still need a way to define the 5x5 splats so that were-elementals are given form. I propose something along these lines for the primary splat, for you to play with as you see fit, BDH:<br /> <br /> <b>- Aerial:</b> Aerial elementals are associated with weather phenomena and other forces of the atmosphere. A raging were-tornado, a noisy were-thunderstorm, and a hell-bent were-snowstorm all are examples of Aerials.<br /> <br /> <b>- Aquatic:</b> Aquatic elementals are creatures that conjure up sea disasters and other phenomena. A were-tsunami (as BDH pointed out), a hungry were-whirlpool, and a crumbling were-glacier are all examples of Aquatics.<br /> <br /> <b>- Agnic:</b> Agnic elementals are the children of fire phenomena. A blazing were-forest fire, a monstrous were-fire tornado, and a sizzling were-lava flow are all examples of Agnics.<br /> <br /> <b>- Aetheric:</b> Aetheric elementals are some of the rarest and most mysterious of elementals, embodying phenomena that comes from the Deep Shadow and space itself. A vicious were-solar flare, a vengeful were-meteor, and a gluttonous were-black hole are all examples of Aetherics.<br /> <br /> <b>- Chthonic:</b> Terran elementals are creatures of the earth, associated with natural disasters found happening on land masses. A slogging were-landslide, a raging were-cave in, and a shifting piece of were-fault line are all examples of Terrans.<br /> <br /> The secondary splat would be similar to tribes, only based on cultural beliefs surrounding the elements; like W:tF, they are associated with elemental systems across the world. I've tried to group them by geographic location. They would be, as follows:<br /> <br /> - <b>Stoicheians:</b> Elementals whose belief and gift systems revolve around the four classical elements, as well as the properties of wet, cold, hot and dry. Their beliefs resemble Grecian attitudes on the elements, and also incorporate beliefs in medieval alchemy.<br /> <br /> - <b>Tattva-Bonans:</b> Elementals whose belief and gift systems revolve around the beliefs presented in Tattva and Bon, from Hinduism/Jainism and Tibetan religion, respectively. Their beliefs resemble the Indian attitudes on these elements.<br /> <br /> - <b>Iluans:</b> Elementals whose belief and gift systems revolve around the Babylonian elements, presented as land, air, sea and sky. They are the oldest of the elemental groups, and resemble Sumerian and Babylonian cultural attitudes on these systems.<br /> <br /> - <b>Mahabhutan Trio:</b> Elementals whose beliefs revolve around the elemental systems of Chinese Wu Xing, Japanese Godai and the Mah\u0101bh\u016bta of Buddhism. Their beliefs are a mix of Chinese, Japanese and Tibetan attitudes on the elements.<br /> <br /> <b>- Wayward:</b> Elementals who do not follow a certain cultural group, but are either highly syncretic, or have their own belief system in life. They are roughly analogous to the Lone Wolves of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, one problem I already see here is writing the culture-based groups in a sensitive way, to avoid the blatant stereotyping seen in W:tF. My solution is that we could scout out for people who have a knowledge of/are part of these cultural groups, and use their expertise to write something that is inoffensive but fantastic at the same time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The next problem, however, is that we don't fit into a universal mold with these ideas. They are all heavily based on a culture, like lodges, and this was just the info I managed to find on well-known elemental systems. We have nothing here representing indigenous ideas on the elements, such as those of the Australian Aborigines or the Native Americans, or ideas from places like African Mythology. If anyone has better ideas for a y-splat, I'm all ears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-11-2015, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T19:38:27-07:00","id":587628,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Y-Splat should focus on how they define a sort of meaning to the primal, chaotic nature of their race? Like, one of these groups draw upon the idea of disasters as punishments from the Heavens and believe themselves to be agents of some sort of divine force/abstract concept, while another embraces the idea that the only meaning is what you give to something, redefining themselves constantly in the hopes of finding something that fits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T20:02:03-07:00","id":587651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=587628#post587628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Y-Splat should focus on how they define a sort of meaning to the primal, chaotic nature of their race? Like, one of these groups draw upon the idea of disasters as punishments from the Heavens and believe themselves to be agents of some sort of divine force/abstract concept, while another embraces the idea that the only meaning is what you give to something, redefining themselves constantly in the hopes of finding something that fits?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds even better to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T20:04:24-07:00","id":587652,"title":"","content":"Why not use the Elemental kith from CotL?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T20:06:09-07:00","id":587655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blunt_Force_Trauma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=587652#post587652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not use the Elemental kith from CotL?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a template, or an option? Not everyone likes the crossover option, nor they do always have the books on hand to rip other things from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-11-2015, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T21:49:44-07:00","id":587697,"title":"","content":"Just pointing out that the concept has been done already albeit in a different line... If you are going to do &quot;were-elementals&quot; what about all the minor sub-sub types (example the filth spirit from the HtV SAS Under the Skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T22:54:47-07:00","id":587718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blunt_Force_Trauma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=587697#post587697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just pointing out that the concept has been done already albeit in a different line... If you are going to do &quot;were-elementals&quot; what about all the minor sub-sub types (example the filth spirit from the HtV SAS Under the Skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that IS true, there is a very big difference between CtL's elementals and the ones theorized here: CtL's elementals are more &quot;the outside looking in&quot;. These elementals are hungry, incredibly alien forces descended from beings FAR older than Urfarah himself. They're the children of natural beings who wiped out the dinosaurs with a single thought. There's a far more Lovecraftian bent to these guys, as well as a more ruthless streak: their Siskur-Dah equivalent is basically on <i>all the time</i>. The urge to break free of human bonds and act as a natural force would would put even a werewolf to shame.<br /> <br /> With that being said, you are correct in that we should look at things like the Filth Spirit from Under the Skin. Elemental spirits have been done before, and we should look at them to gain ideas on what a shifter based on them would be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T04:05:25-07:00","id":588009,"title":"","content":"Ideally were-elementals should resemble elemental changelings to the same extent that werewolves resemble beast changelings. <br /> <br /> Which is to say, superficially at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T04:18:40-07:00","id":588011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=587718#post587718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These elementals are hungry, incredibly alien forces descended from beings FAR older than Urfarah himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a thing there, right, because-<br /> <br /> Curses at the situation in which I must still sadly hold my tongue :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T07:50:51-07:00","id":588138,"title":"","content":"Alright, so if we're going the were-route we should probably consider shifting issues. Do you think they should have equivalents of all 5 forms? <br /> <br /> Obviously human and near-human are fairly easy to do, but the other 3 are a bit trickier. I was thinking of a sort of pure element form, a bigger humanoid-elemental form and a short-lived ragey natural disaster form to mirror urhan, urshul and gauru, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:05:31-07:00","id":588146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=588138#post588138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so if we're going the were-route we should probably consider shifting issues. Do you think they should have equivalents of all 5 forms?<br /> <br /> Obviously human and near-human are fairly easy to do, but the other 3 are a bit trickier. I was thinking of a sort of pure element form, a bigger humanoid-elemental form and a short-lived ragey natural disaster form to mirror urhan, urshul and gauru, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. As for near-human and &quot;near-disaster&quot;, the near-human form manifests as things like flaming eyes or a lower body made of water \u2014 things meant to show off tidbits of an elemental's true power. I also think that, in a change-up of the usual, it's the natural form that has a time limit as opposed to the Gauru. It would be game-breaking otherwise to have a wildfire form that blazes through a forest for as many turns as you want.<br /> <br /> Acrozatarim, stop making me squee! xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:35:10-07:00","id":588158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=588146#post588146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same here. As for near-human and &quot;near-disaster&quot;, the near-human form manifests as things like flaming eyes or a lower body made of water \u2014 things meant to show off tidbits of an elemental's true power. I also think that, in a change-up of the usual, it's the natural form that has a time limit as opposed to the Gauru. It would be game-breaking otherwise to have a wildfire form that blazes through a forest for as many turns as you want.<br /> <br /> Acrozatarim, stop making me squee! xD</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, scaling the intensity of the elemental effect would be the thing to separate forms. The Swarm Form merit from Strix would be a good starting point, which is why I used it for converting Changing Breeds. The real question is how would you divy up powers and what would be the perks of their non-Lunar lineage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T10:16:00-07:00","id":588266,"title":"","content":"Yeah, fire's a tricky one. For water I was thinking the urhan form would just be an ambulatory puddle. Nothing too dangerous there. But for fire a similar form could cause a lot of damage very easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T10:43:50-07:00","id":588283,"title":"","content":"What about a system of Primal Urge = intensity of the urhan equivalent? Such as thus:<br /> <br /> PU 1 = Puddle, campfire-sized patch of fire, ball lightning, large boulder<br /> PU 2 = Large puddle, bonfire-sized fire, small burst of lightning strike, falling patch of cliff<br /> PU 3 = Small pond, small car-sized patch of fire, 1-minute intense, localized chain lightning, a minor landslide off a small cliff<br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T10:51:07-07:00","id":588314,"title":"","content":"Or, or maybe we could say that if you take the form of a small patch of fire, you will <i>remain</i> in the form of a small patch of fire. No spreading, at least without spending essence. That would leave the time limit open for the destructive force of nature that is gauru form, as it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:18:33-07:00","id":588323,"title":"","content":"Sounds reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> Now personally all I can think of is a B-Movie plot where a werewolf transforms into a flame and those burned by this elemental shall become were-elementals themselves. Like &quot;Curse of the Were-Elemental! Now in 3-D!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T17:30:56-07:00","id":588614,"title":"","content":"Maybe applying Environmental Tilts in Urshul, while gaining element-appropriate buffs in other forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:40:47-07:00","id":588693,"title":"","content":"And here I'm comfortable with making fetishes that grant the elemental dread powers of claimed off elemental gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:49:02-07:00","id":588697,"title":"","content":"You could probably get something out of the <i>Become The Primal Foundation</i> clause of the Contracts Of Elements as inspiration for the pure elemental form rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-13-2015, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T05:23:56-07:00","id":589042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=587568#post587568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, if we drop the four elements splat idea, we still need a way to define the 5x5 splats so that were-elementals are given form. I propose something along these lines for the primary splat, for you to play with as you see fit, BDH:<br /> <br /> <b>- Aerial:</b> Aerial elementals are associated with weather phenomena and other forces of the atmosphere. A raging were-tornado, a noisy were-thunderstorm, and a hell-bent were-snowstorm all are examples of Aerials.<br /> <br /> <b>- Aquatic:</b> Aquatic elementals are creatures that conjure up sea disasters and other phenomena. A were-tsunami (as BDH pointed out), a hungry were-whirlpool, and a crumbling were-glacier are all examples of Aquatics.<br /> <br /> <b>- Agnic:</b> Agnic elementals are the children of fire phenomena. A blazing were-forest fire, a monstrous were-fire tornado, and a sizzling were-lava flow are all examples of Agnics.<br /> <br /> <b>- Aetheric:</b> Aetheric elementals are some of the rarest and most mysterious of elementals, embodying phenomena that comes from the Deep Shadow and space itself. A vicious were-solar flare, a vengeful were-meteor, and a gluttonous were-black hole are all examples of Aetherics.<br /> <br /> <b>- Chthonic:</b> Terran elementals are creatures of the earth, associated with natural disasters found happening on land masses. A slogging were-landslide, a raging were-cave in, and a shifting piece of were-fault line are all examples of Terrans.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like these, as long as individual characters didn't have to be narrowed down to, &quot;this character is a [were-cave in]&quot; or &quot;I'm a [were-meteor strike]!&quot; It gets too limiting. But yeah, I like it. The Aetheric was a nice touch.<br /> <br /> For forms, I think maybe we compact: what about three forms? Human. Elemental. DISASTER.<br /> <br /> <i>Hishu </i>is their <i>hishu</i>. Simple enough. Human means human.<br /> <i>Hardunsuath </i>is their <i>urhan</i> and it gives them spirit stats (derived from their normal ones) and certain advantages only spirits get (no wound penalties, etc.).<br /> [Disaster/Cataclysm/Chaos] is their <i>gauru</i> and it is a physical manifestation of their core nature. Even being near it is a problem because it lashes out on its own, compelled to enact elemental chaos.<br /> <br /> Like BDH commented, we talked about compulsion-type stuff. Maybe each character has a compulsion they must fulfill every scene, every week, whatever. If they don't, they risk their own <i>kuruth</i>. Maybe Agnics need to burn things, Cthonics need to bury them, Aetheric... need to... be outerspacey, I don't know! Heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T06:32:29-07:00","id":589127,"title":"","content":"Thoughts:<br /> <br /> Maybe even taking their hybrid form starts to cause minor natural disasters associated with them, and if they rage, they just get worse. Spontaenous thunderstorms, etc. They don't just become these things, they manifest them in their immediate vicinity (and the more powerful they are, the broader their range and more destructive the force). This can be tempered by living in places opposite to their natures (though for some it's more difficult than others) like an Aquatic living in the desert. Of course, this comes with its own problems...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T15:53:10-07:00","id":589604,"title":"","content":"Beyond destruction, what is the theme here? How do these creatures blend in with humanity. What is their purpose, goals, etc... And Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T16:20:59-07:00","id":589617,"title":"","content":"I expected a much dumber thread here, and instead find awesomeness.<br /> <br /> As you were people, as you were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T16:36:16-07:00","id":589624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blunt_Force_Trauma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=589604#post589604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond destruction, what is the theme here? How do these creatures blend in with humanity. What is their purpose, goals, etc... And Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>One idea I've had is that, in contrast to the Uratha, the Elementals don't actually know that mutch about their mythic past, and have no clue as to why they were made. Though the Y-Splats would provide their own explinations, they have no big, default myth and purpose to anchor themselves to. After all, humanity has sought the meaning in disasters and tragedy since our oldest ancestors were able to think &quot;Why?&quot; Just because the Elementals <i>are</i> the disaster in question doesn't mean they're as clueless as the rest of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:08:58-07:00","id":589659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=589624#post589624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I've had is that, in contrast to the Uratha, the Elementals don't actually know that mutch about their mythic past, and have no clue as to why they were made. Though the Y-Splats would provide their own explinations, they have no big, default myth and purpose to anchor themselves to. After all, humanity has sought the meaning in disasters and tragedy since our oldest ancestors were able to think &quot;Why?&quot; Just because the Elementals <i>are</i> the disaster in question doesn't mean they're as clueless as the rest of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could say elementals are very much the lost, angry, neglected children of the forces that spawned them. Mother Moon and Father Wolf at least gave their pups a purpose; the elementals have been left to find their place as they see fit. As natural forces, their progenitors don't do as they do because of some sort of duty, bargain, or oath, but exist because they just...are.<br /> <br /> If were-elementals weren't part human, and had the blue-and-orange mindset of their progenitors, they'd understand that. They aren't, and have no reason or rhyme handed down to them from their spirit-gods as to what they're supposed to doing in life, save for existing. The response from their progenitors is an overall &quot;meh&quot;. That's why their Siskur Dah equivalent could be on all the time: they aren't hunting for a certain prey, they're hunting for purpose itself, and are driven towards that. That natural drive, however, is rooted partially in the need to know, and their spirit halves desperately trying to just <i>be</i>, because they're <i>supposed</i> to just be. Such is rote and routine nature of the Hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T20:19:50-07:00","id":589830,"title":"","content":"On a side note in regards to a fire were-elemental, I think of the Dr Who episode Burn with Me...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T05:48:08-07:00","id":590166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=589659#post589659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One could say elementals are very much the lost, angry, neglected children of the forces that spawned them. Mother Moon and Father Wolf at least gave their pups a purpose; the elementals have been left to find their place as they see fit. As natural forces, their progenitors don't do as they do because of some sort of duty, bargain, or oath, but exist because they just...are.<br /> <br /> If were-elementals weren't part human, and had the blue-and-orange mindset of their progenitors, they'd understand that. They aren't, and have no reason or rhyme handed down to them from their spirit-gods as to what they're supposed to doing in life, save for existing. The response from their progenitors is an overall &quot;meh&quot;. That's why their Siskur Dah equivalent could be on all the time: they aren't hunting for a certain prey, they're hunting for purpose itself, and are driven towards that. That natural drive, however, is rooted partially in the need to know, and their spirit halves desperately trying to just <i>be</i>, because they're <i>supposed</i> to just be. Such is rote and routine nature of the Hisil.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. It would also be cool if their Y-Splast was all about <i>how</i> they go about trying to find their purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T07:53:07-07:00","id":590204,"title":"","content":"I am intrigued by this project.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to include a plant/life angle, don't discount the devastating effect of invasive species on regions. Kudzu choking out native plant life, molds spreading across every surface, plagues that decimate populations. Life thriving without a thought to delicate pre-existing ecosystems until the entire web collapses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T09:35:50-07:00","id":590266,"title":"","content":"espritdecalmar: Much like how three more options for tribes + the Bale Hounds were eventually added in as plot potential, a sidebar could be made about new elementals embodying forces related to animals, diseases (like bacteria/viruses) and plants. No doubt there would be some confusion over the appearance of such elementals, since the spirit-gods that birthed the original five had had nothing to say (as usual) on the matter. Delicious WTF reactions would probably be across the board.<br /> <br /> @gebbethine: Way ahead of you, there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>The Paragons:</b> Paragon elementals believe that the existence of their powers is for the greater good at all. Whether it's an Aerial acting as a helpful meteorologist, bringing much-needed weather (such as rain) to needy parts of their country, or an Agnic who tries to redirect forest fires away from people's homes, Paragons are all about the pursuit of helping others and the world. They find purpose in the survival of the planet and humanity through altruism, charity, and the protection of the innocent and weak.<br /> <br /> <b>The Conquerors:</b> Conqueror elementals, in stark contrast to the Paragons, believe in the use of their powers to solely stay on top of the heap. They are tyrants, kings and overlords, whether it's an angry were-whirlpool demanding virgin tribute from passing sailors, or a Chthonic that will bring down a mountain on a tiny village if he is not worshipped as a god. Conquerors are all about the pursuit of power and keeping it, subjugating anyone under their heel they do not see as worthy or equal.<br /> <br /> <b>The Watchers:</b> Watcher elementals believe themselves to be the keepers of Law and Promise. Their moral codes and rules of conduct do not have to make sense \u2014 they are the guardians, policemen and governors of myriad mortal and occult secrets, oaths and societies. One Aquatic may be a part of the Coast Guard, bringing in illegal waste dumpers with the power of the waves; another may be an Aerial hunting down mages, feeling their manipulation of weather violates Nature's Law. Watchers pursue order in the universe, and go to great lengths to keep it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Unfettered:</b> Unfettered elementals revel in chaos. They are crazed, unpredictable, the most inhuman in thought and behaviour of all the elemental kin. One may be an Agnic that lights houses on fire every Tuesday, then lights people on fire every Friday just to see what that might do. Another may be an earth elemental who causes earthquakes in the middle of nowhere, laughing as scientists try to scramble and explain the devastation. The Unfettered's pursuit is doing whatever they want, and succeeding whenever they get away with it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pathless:</b> Pathless elementals do not follow any set of purpose. Instead, they are a loose collective of elementals whose ideals, ethics and goals do not fit neatly within the other established groups, or are not liked by certain individuals. Their purpose lies in whatever they find becomes it, whether it's an Agnic lighting lamps in Victorian-era London to an Aetheric providing clues to the nature of space to a little-known astronomer. The Pathless have many pursuits, but all of them are not as clear-cut as those from the other four groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T10:42:11-07:00","id":590299,"title":"","content":"@Sikla: I like some of what you're doing here, but they seem necessarily, diametrically opposed to one another. Assuming that we want mixed groups, we'd have to explain why in any of the hells Paragons and Conquerors or Unfettered would hang out together. Let alone in the same...oh man, we need to think of a group name. Anyway, in the same party.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, these don't have to be the Y-splats. They could be akin to the Forsaken or Pure: Broader cultural groups that will have subdivisions based on more specific ideological concerns.<br /> <br /> The subdivisions could be like the Tribes: Based around how they try to manage their Obsessions and Compulsions. And not to mention how they interact with the <i>Hisil</i>. How do the <i>ilthum</i> respond to these half-flesh disasters walking around? Do swarms of chaotic spirits swim in their wake? Do the elementals encourage or deplore it when that happens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T11:38:39-07:00","id":590359,"title":"","content":"Well, what Sikla presented sort of IS like the Tribes. They each decided what their <i>purpose</i> is, and follow it.<br /> <br /> I like it. They don't have to all be able to work together. Look at Vampire Covenants: you'd be hard-pressed to find a Crone and a Snactified anywhere near each other amicably.<br /> <br /> Another, similar idea is that they each decide what they <i>are</i>. Are they gods? Are they servants? Are they blessed? Are they cursed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T12:08:13-07:00","id":590382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=590299#post590299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Sikla: I like some of what you're doing here, but they seem necessarily, diametrically opposed to one another. Assuming that we want mixed groups, we'd have to explain why in any of the hells Paragons and Conquerors or Unfettered would hang out together. Let alone in the same...oh man, we need to think of a group name. Anyway, in the same party.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, these don't have to be the Y-splats. They could be akin to the Forsaken or Pure: Broader cultural groups that will have subdivisions based on more specific ideological concerns.<br /> <br /> The subdivisions could be like the Tribes: Based around how they try to manage their Obsessions and Compulsions. And not to mention how they interact with the <i>Hisil</i>. How do the <i>ilthum</i> respond to these half-flesh disasters walking around? Do swarms of chaotic spirits swim in their wake? Do the elementals encourage or deplore it when that happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Them working as z-splat is fine to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for the y-splat, why not have Gebbethine's idea of what they <i>are</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T16:20:43-07:00","id":590570,"title":"","content":"Thoughts On Y-Splats<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">My thoughts on the subject, expanding on from what I said before, is that each Y-Splat offers a different narrative/explanation for what the Elementals are and why. I'm also reminded of the Mage Order spoiler where it was offhandedly mentioned that the Vampire Covenants act as a way to tether a Kindred to Humanity in some way, that each of the Y-Splats might do something similar, giving an Elemental an extra drive/ideal that helps to keep them human. Though it doesn't need to be spelled out in the final product, let's just call it a &quot;Calling&quot; for now. To give examples expanding off the ideas I mentioned earlier, complete with (probably stupid) provisionary names;<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Chosen&quot;- Though the details may change from member to member, the core structure of the narrative remains the same. Long ago, [Higher Power(s)] looked down upon the world and was displeased, and so created the Elementals to act as the agents of [his/her/its/their] will. From the kindly landslide that guards and guides the members of a small ethnic community in the name of their god to the maddened vacuum that slaughters anyone who seeks the truths That Man Was Not Meant To Know, the Chosen are the most purpose driven of the Elementals, laser-focused on what they believe needs to be done. Their &quot;Calling&quot; is Duty; a disaster may be powerful, but it lacks the ability to control or direct its power as it should. The Chosen believe that Elementals are divine agents, not divine weapons, and should comport themselves as such.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;The Thousand Signs&quot;- This group is odd in the sense that they are defined by their <b>lack</b> of a narrative. Maybe they were created for some purpose, or just because, or maybe they just always existed, but whatever it was, the Signers say, simply doesn't matter. In the end, what happened in the long-lost past doesn't have a whit to do with the price of beans in China. You aren't defined by some ancient narrative, you define <b>yourself!</b> Fire can mean purification or destruction, water can give life or destroy it; in the end, your nature is what you make of it. The Signers study and swap ideas, meanings, and stories, redefining themselves again and again until they find something truly them. Their &quot;Calling&quot; is Understanding; a landslide can't be anything other than a landslide, a tornado can't decide if it harms or heals. To surrender to your nature is to be defined by another, and that is something the Signers simply cannot allow.<br /> <br /> Another idea might include a group of self-proclaimed Demigods(either in the sense of being titanic Pangeans fractured into many mortal vessels or human bloodlines infused with power by the gods of the Shadow) who believe that their purpose is to grow stronger and eventually ascend, becoming world-shaking Spirits still capable of feeling and reasoning with the full range of humanity, something far greater than their progenitors.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, how stupid is this idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Sometimes I Really HATE the fact I mostly use my phone to surf the web 07-14-2015, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T07:50:59-07:00","id":592615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=590570#post590570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts On Y-Splats<br /> <br /> <i>--snip--</i><br /> <br /> So, how stupid is this idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not stupid at all: I really like it. Choosing their own direction should be a big deal to these guys. And it mixes nicely with gebbethine's idea. I'd totally play an Aerial Signer for instance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:08:22-07:00","id":592872,"title":"","content":"It works as a Pure vs. Forsaken division.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T20:54:34-07:00","id":601358,"title":"","content":"Count me in, but one thing that's come to my attention is how do we... justify these Were-Elemantals existing. I assume they're partially spirit beings, similar to werewolves (as that's the thread), but I sincerely doubt that any of it involved traditional reproduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:09:11-07:00","id":606594,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm gonna do it&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dave, no...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm gonna fuck the bonfire&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Dave</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T21:30:02-07:00","id":607480,"title":"","content":"I'd venture to guess that the DA origin story would be a hard sell, but as for modern members, somewhere between the Hulk, the First Change, and the Homecoming would be a good device for becoming. Kind of a &quot;3 days to touch the soul before it consumes you&quot; deal, an incident involving your element drives you to the brink of death and in that moment, you see the world and yourself for what they are, and achieve the modicum of personal enlightenment necessary to make the change. Genetics play a small roll in determining the potential for change, but it really comes down to a defining moment of clarity, on par on with the First Change.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T21:51:27-07:00","id":607487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/584885-were-elementals?p=607480#post607480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd venture to guess that the DA origin story would be a hard sell, but as for modern members, somewhere between the Hulk, the First Change, and the Homecoming would be a good device for becoming. Kind of a &quot;3 days to touch the soul before it consumes you&quot; deal, an incident involving your element drives you to the brink of death and in that moment, you see the world and yourself for what they are, and achieve the modicum of personal enlightenment necessary to make the change. Genetics play a small roll in determining the potential for change, but it really comes down to a defining moment of clarity, on par on with the First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think this is the most apropos. One side believes it's a divine vision, the other sees it more as the realization you're not fully human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}